# CLARA Training Commands — Linux / ROCm / Distrobox

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[distrobox enter clara-training] --> B[export HSA_OVERRIDE=11.0.0]
    B --> C[source ~/clara-training/venv/bin/activate]
    C --> D{Smoke Test?}
    D -->|Yes| E[bash scripts/smoke_test.sh]
    D -->|No| F{Has Checkpoint?}
    F -->|No| G[Phase 1 Fresh Start]
    F -->|Yes, resume| H[Phase 1 Resume]
    G --> I[ONNX Export]
    H --> I
    I --> J[ctest --output-on-failure]
    E --> G
```

## Prerequisites

```bash
# Enter distrobox (already created)
distrobox enter clara-training

# Activate venv
source ~/clara-training/venv/bin/activate

# ROCm env vars (MANDATORY on Strix Point 860M — NOT on MI300X)
export HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=11.0.0
export HSA_ENABLE_SDMA=0
export PYTORCH_ALLOC_CONF="garbage_collection_threshold:0.8,max_split_size_mb:256"
export MIOPEN_FIND_MODE=5
```

**MI300X only:** Do NOT set `HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION`. ROCm detects gfx942 natively.
```bash
export PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF="expandable_segments:True"
```

## Quick Smoke Test

Verifies the full pipeline end-to-end with synthetic data (~2 min):

```bash
# From inside distrobox, with venv active + HSA_OVERRIDE set
cd "/var/home/sgm/Github Repo's/clara"
bash scripts/smoke_test.sh
```

**What it tests:** Synthetic WAV generation → 10 training steps → ONNX export → onnxruntime verify.

## Phase 1 Identity Training

### Fresh Start (no checkpoint)

```bash
python train_clara_parallel.py \
  --data ~/datasets/musdb18hq/train \
  --device cuda \
  --batch 4 \
  --grad-accum 4 \
  --steps 50000 \
  --clip-seconds 0.5 \
  --ckpt-every 500 \
  --val-every 500 \
  --log-every 25 \
  --num-workers 0 \
  --cache
```

### MI300X Config (big batches, long clips)

```bash
python train_clara_parallel.py \
  --data ~/datasets/musdb18hq/train \
  --device cuda \
  --batch 64 \
  --grad-accum 2 \
  --steps 50000 \
  --clip-seconds 2.0 \
  --ckpt-every 1000 \
  --val-every 1000 \
  --log-every 25 \
  --num-workers 8 \
  --cache
```

### Resume from Checkpoint

```bash
python train_clara_parallel.py \
  --data ~/datasets/musdb18hq/train \
  --resume checkpoints_clara/checkpoint_025000.pt \
  --resume-optimizer \
  --device cuda
```

## GPU Monitoring

Run in a **separate terminal** (inside distrobox, with rocm-smi installed):

```bash
# Live GPU stats — temp, power, utilization, memory
watch -n 2 rocm_smi --showtemp --showpower --showuse --showmemuse

# Quick GPU check
rocm-smi

# PyTorch GPU check (no rocm-smi required)
python -c "import torch; print(f'GPU: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}'); print(f'Mem: {torch.cuda.memory_allocated()/1e9:.2f} GB')"
```

**Install rocm-smi in distrobox (one-time):**
```bash
sudo apt-get install rocm-smi
```

## ONNX Export

After training completes:

```bash
python train_clara_export.py \
  --checkpoint checkpoints_clara/final.pt \
  --output models/mamba_rt.onnx \
  --seq-len 64
```

## Verify in C++ Engine

```bash
cmake -B build -DBUILD_TESTING=ON && cmake --build build --parallel && ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
```

