## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------|-----|
| Hang at "GPU warmup" | MIOpen compilation deadlock on first forward pass | Fixed — warmup now uses 1 chunk (64 samples). If still hanging: `sudo fuser /dev/kfd && sudo pkill -9 -f train_clara` |
| `rocm-smi: command not found` | Not installed in distrobox | `sudo apt-get install rocm-smi` (one-time) |
| `CUDA not available` | Missing `HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION` | `export HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION=11.0.0` |
| NaN at step 8 | bfloat16 AMP on 860M ROCm (known issue) | Don't use `--amp` on this hardware. Default is float32. |
| HIP error | Wrong ROCm env | Set `HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION` before Python import |
| OOM | Batch too large for APU shared memory | Reduce `--batch` or `--clip-seconds` |
| Slow training (~3 step/s) | Chunked SSM scan on iGPU | Expected on 860M. Use MI300X for production runs. |

